<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds were following Spain higher in fairly illiquid trade and traders expected the Spanish market to continue set the pace.</p>
<p>Traders did not see the announcement of details of the government's 1997 budget package, to be sent to parliament on Tuesday, as having any great impact on trading. The main numbers of the plan are already known.</p>
<p>They saw the spread between the Portuguese and Spanish 10-year cash market remaining around 10 basis points.</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbonn bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
